{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"insanitary-divine-moa","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` is a pure re-export shim over the stdlib-only\nleaf `rebar._ids`. Its own docstring records why: the resolution primitives moved DOWN\nto `rebar._ids` so `rebar.reducer` could depend on them without reaching UP into\n`_engine_support`, which was a layering inversion and an import cycle. The shim was kept\nonly so existing importers would not have to change, and it says so: \"New code should\nimport from `rebar._ids` directly.\"\n\nADR 0111 forbids internal shims. This one is the largest remaining instance.\n\nMeasured on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d`:\n\n- The shim re-exports exactly 9 names, every one of them under the SAME name it has in\n  `rebar._ids`: `_FULL_ID_RE`, `_JIRA_KEY_RE`, `_SHORT_ID_RE`,\n  `_resolve_via_binding_store`, `_scan_alias`, `build_alias_index`,\n  `build_resolver_scan_index`, `resolve_ticket_dir_name`, `resolve_ticket_id`. It adds no\n  behavior — the module body is imports and `__all__`.\n- 51 files import it: 31 under `src/`, 19 under `tests/`, 1 under `scripts/`. The\n  heaviest clusters are `src/rebar/_commands` (12), `tests/unit` (8), and\n  `src/rebar/_engine_support` itself (7).\n- No file names the shim as a string. `git grep -F` for `'rebar._engine_support.resolver'`\n  and the double-quoted form across `src tests scripts` returns nothing, so there is no\n  `monkeypatch.setattr`, `importlib`, or `getattr` site that a static rewrite would miss.\n\nBecause every re-exported name is identical on both sides and nothing reaches the module\ndynamically, the migration is a module-path rewrite with no symbol renaming and no\ncall-site restructuring.\n\n## Change\n\nRewrite the module path in all 51 importers: `rebar._engine_support.resolver` becomes\n`rebar._ids`. Imported names are unchanged. Where a file already imports from\n`rebar._ids`, merge the two import statements rather than leaving a duplicate.\n\nThen delete `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py`.\n\nExtend the held-out shim oracle `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py`, which\nalready establishes the convention for this repo: assert the shim module is gone AND\nthat the canonical path still resolves, so the test cannot pass vacuously by everything\nbeing absent.\n\n## Testing\n\n- A new case in `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py` asserting\n  `importlib.import_module(\"rebar._engine_support.resolver\")` raises `ModuleNotFoundError`,\n  and that `rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_id` still resolves a known ticket id — the\n  positive half that keeps the assertion non-vacuous.\n- The existing resolver test suites are untouched and must stay green; they exercise the\n  same functions through `rebar._ids`.\n- `make verify` is the contract for the whole-tree effect, including the import-convention\n  guard, which is the gate that would catch a malformed rewrite.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `git grep -cF -e '_engine_support.resolver' -e '_engine_support import resolver' -- src tests scripts`\n      prints nothing and exits 1. Before this change it lists 51 files.\n- [ ] **AC2** `test -e src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` exits 1.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python -c \"import importlib; importlib.import_module('rebar._engine_support.resolver')\"`\n      exits non-zero with `ModuleNotFoundError`.\n- [ ] **AC4** `python -c \"from rebar._ids import _FULL_ID_RE, _JIRA_KEY_RE, _SHORT_ID_RE, _resolve_via_binding_store, _scan_alias, build_alias_index, build_resolver_scan_index, resolve_ticket_dir_name, resolve_ticket_id\"`\n      exits 0, proving all 9 formerly re-exported names remain reachable at the canonical\n      leaf.\n- [ ] **AC5** `ruff check src tests scripts` exits 0 with no output, proving no import was\n      left unused or duplicated by the rewrite.\n- [ ] **AC6** `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py` gains a case covering this\n      shim, and `pytest tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py -q` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC7** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD` touches only the 51 importers,\n      the deleted shim, `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py` and\n      `docs/release-notes.md`, and no other path.\n- [ ] **AC8** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Ordering\n\nIndependent of the `_processors` re-export story — different modules, no shared source\nfile. Either may land first. Both are prerequisites for epic `e12f`'s alias-deletion\nstory.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The `reducer/_processors.py` re-exports, which are a different shape (names forwarded\n  from two sibling modules, not a whole-module shim) and are tracked on their own ticket.\n- Any behavior change in `rebar._ids`. This change moves import paths only; the\n  resolution semantics are untouched.\n- `docs/` prose that mentions the old path in historical narrative, and\n  `docs/release-notes.md`, which names retired paths by design.","id":"2207-e956-c937-4e8c","parent_id":"e12f-a994-29d3-4f72","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate resolver shim importers to rebar._ids and delete the shim"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793377691239868031,"uuid":"06065fc4-7bb6-41fc-851a-0dd4b75b8983"}